        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(auto-reply): add \"commentary\" verbose level for narration-only progress",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`/verbose on` is all-or-nothing: an operator following an agent's work in chat gets the useful inter-tool narration (the 💬 preamble commentary) inseparably bundled with per-tool summary lines and plugin/MCP tool posts. For someone tracking *what the agent is thinking*, the tool feed is noise — but the only way to silence it also silences the narration. Closes #103170.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe narration and the tool posts are already independent delivery paths in the dispatch layer; they were just wired to a single boolean. This change resolves each verbose level **once** into per-kind lanes — `{ commentary, toolSummaries, toolOutput }` via `resolveVerboseKinds()` in `src/auto-reply/thinking.shared.ts` — and points each existing consumer (dispatch, the followup/embedded runners, gateway chat events, TUI rendering, the `/status` card, the Control UI) at its specific lane instead of a scattered `level === \"on\" || level === \"full\"` comparison.\n\nA fourth preset, **`commentary`**, enables only the narration lane. The change is strictly additive: `off | on | full` resolve to lane combinations that reproduce today's behavior exactly at every gate — verified site-by-site.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- **`/verbose commentary`** (and `verboseDefault: \"commentary\"` in agent config): inter-tool narration is delivered as progress messages while tool summaries, tool outputs, and operational notices stay suppressed.\n- Existing levels and aliases are unchanged. Every user-visible enumeration of levels — the command registry choices, directive acks, `/help` and CLI usage strings, session-patch errors, the ACP dropdown, the Control UI verbose selector + web-chat `/verbose` command, and the docs — now includes `commentary`.\n- Two intentional edges: `commentary` omits run-failure detail that `on` shows (that detail rides the `toolSummaries` lane); and the followup runner's fallback gate now normalizes its level input, so a garbage fallback value no longer counts as verbose-enabled (a latent bug fixed in passing).\n- The `isCommentary` **final-payload** opt-in (`commentaryPayloadsEnabled`) is deliberately kept distinct from the commentary **progress** lane — verbose level never enables final commentary payloads, matching direct dispatch on the queued path too.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm build` and `pnpm check` both exit 0 (typecheck + oxlint + policy guards); `docs/.generated/config-baseline.sha256` regenerated via `pnpm config:docs:gen`; `CHANGELOG.md` untouched per CONTRIBUTING.\n- New/updated tests across the touched surface: the level→kinds resolver and presets (`thinking.test.ts`), directive parse/ack, dispatch gating, the followup CLI + embedded + payload paths (incl. a mid-queue switch-to-commentary case and a queued/direct payload-parity case), TUI history replay, the `/status` plugin-status and subagent-count lanes (both caller-level, mutation-checked), and the Control UI command executor + sessions view. Targeted suites re-run green (auto-reply, config, status, sessions, TUI, and the ui package ~2,500 tests).\n- Every non-lane verbose boolean across `src/`, `extensions/`, and `ui/` was audited for parity; the remaining `!== \"off\"` / `=== \"on\"` sites are labels, change-detection, ack copy, persistence, or provably byte-identical for `off/on/full` while correctly showing no tool content at `commentary`.\n\nVerified on Node 24; re-validated on a second checkout at current `main`. **Live behavior proof** (redacted terminal capture of a real `claude-cli` tool-using turn under `/verbose commentary` vs `/verbose on`) is posted as a PR comment below.\n\nNote: a couple of hunks in `thinking.test.ts` are `oxfmt`-driven (the file on `main` fails `oxfmt --check`); reverting them fails the formatter.\n\n## Upgrade & Mixed-Version Compatibility\n\n`commentary` is an **additive** value on an existing string enum (`verboseDefault` in config, `verboseLevel` on the session entry). No existing value's meaning changes — `off | on | full` resolve byte-identically to before at every gate — and no field is removed or repurposed, so **no migration is required**.\n\nMixed-version / downgrade behavior (verified against the pre-feature normalizer): an older runtime or client that reads a persisted `verboseLevel: \"commentary\"` treats it as an unrecognized level — `normalizeVerboseLevel()` returns `undefined` (it falls through to the default `return undefined`), so the session resolves to its configured default rather than throwing. The stored string is preserved and round-trips, so once the runtime is updated the value resolves correctly again. New code reading old persisted values behaves exactly as today.\n\nNet: forward-compatible (old values unchanged), backward-tolerant (unknown value degrades gracefully to the default, never a crash or data loss), migration-free.\n\n## AI-Assisted Disclosure\n\nThis PR was authored with AI assistance (Claude, via Claude Code) — reflected in the commit's `Co-Authored-By` trailer.\n\n- [x] Marked as AI-assisted\n- [x] Author has reviewed the full diff and understands what the code does\n- [x] `codex review --base origin/main` was run locally before opening, and findings were addressed across several rounds before this PR was published: the per-kind lane split, queued-followup commentary (CLI + embedded), TUI history replay, operational-notice gating, and the `/status` plugin-status and subagent-count leaks\n- [x] Will resolve or reply to bot review conversations after addressing them\n\nSession logs available on request.\n",
